mean |lag| 190 steps = 1.33 tone periods, but only 0.38 of one correlation window
=> aligned and elapsed windows share 62% of their samples on average; 70% of pair-segments share half or more, 2% are disjoint
=> the alignment contrast D is attenuated by construction: the registered
   +-300-step jitter is SMALLER than the 500-step readout window, so the two
   clocks are not independent views.  A decisive rerun needs either
   jitter >= 1000 steps (disjoint windows) or a window shorter than the jitter.
